From ea1e424667d75581af2d3cd1707351bc0d5abdd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:45:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] target/microblaze: enter sleep mode on hibernate

LOCAL ONLY: not for submission to qemu-devel (QEMU AI policy).
Reference for a hand-written fix.

trans_mbar halts the CPU only when bit 16 of IMM is set:

	if (mbar_imm & 16) {

UG984 (mbar) enters sleep mode when either of the two most significant
IMM bits is set, "if (IMM & 24) != 0", and Table 69 defines the
pseudo-instructions sleep, hibernate and suspend as mbar 16, 8 and 24.
hibernate, mbar 8, therefore runs straight on instead of halting until
an interrupt.

Test IMM & 24.  The privilege check keeps covering all three: UG984's
list of privileged instructions names SLEEP, HIBERNATE and SUSPEND.
The mbar page itself says the instruction is privileged when the most
significant IMM bit is set, which would leave hibernate unprivileged;
I followed the list, so that a user-mode program cannot halt the CPU.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/microblaze/translate.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/microblaze/translate.c b/target/microblaze/translate.c
index fefe5cb55..f16a288be 100644
--- a/target/microblaze/translate.c
+++ b/target/microblaze/translate.c
@@ -1232,10 +1232,10 @@ static bool trans_mbar(DisasContext *dc, arg_mbar *arg)
         tcg_gen_mb(TCG_BAR_SC | TCG_MO_ALL);
     }
 
-    /* Sleep. */
-    if (mbar_imm & 16) {
+    /* Sleep (16), hibernate (8) or suspend (24).  */
+    if (mbar_imm & 24) {
         if (trap_userspace(dc, true)) {
-            /* Sleep is a privileged instruction.  */
+            /* All three are privileged instructions.  */
             return true;
         }
 
